commit 75d37016a9e0cbfcbd4925d91343ffb13e902e3d

C03: a mind-validated unsupported reply is exempt from the App's failure-language veto (UI1661)

UI1659 measured «Go to the announcements channel in Discord.»: the mind closed the turn as a known unsupported effect and its bounded contract validated «I cannot go to the announcements channel in Discord as requested.», but UserMessagePolicy rejected it as failure language — its request-text heuristic (ConversationFallbackIntent) does not see the mind's limit — and the generic fallback was published without the request. The conversation kind now reaches the policy (unsupportedByMind) and exempts that reply from looks_like_failure; every other check still applies.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>


